{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"bsltxy3mh","tool_use_id":"toolu_01ETjHuBMdCfd7AYgB3EJcba","status":"completed","output_file":"/tmp/claude-441489/-scratch-users-kushinm-auto-psych-outer-loop-live-runs-run2-repo/3dce34f6-6e85-412b-9be4-6e3bf4af1a3e/tasks/bsltxy3mh.output","summary":"Background command \"D=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_4/candidate_0\ncat > $D/hypothesis.md << 'EOF'\nPeople read a sequence flip by flip while keeping a running tally of how far heads lead tails, and they expect a random coin's lead to keep changing hands: the tally should drift away from even and then come back, again and again. A sequence in which one face stays ahead for a long unbroken stretch — the tally leaving even and not getting back for many flips, even if it never strays far (HHTHTHTH stays one or two heads ahead throughout) — looks like a coin stuck in favour of one face and so less random, by a shared penalty on the longest stretch the lead is held without a return to even (as a share of the length). The rest of the impression is the current best model's (tally span against a personal expected span, switching against a personal ideal rate, chunk variety and a rule-built penalty scaled by a personal pattern sensitivity, the final-streak penalty, a personal left/right lean); the claim is that the duration of a held lead, not only how far the tally swings, counts against randomness.\nEOF\necho held_lead_duration_tally > $D/model_name.txt\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop\npython3 - << 'EOF'\nsrc=open(\"models/terminal_streak_recency_pattern_rule.py\").read()\ndoc_end=src.index('\"\"\"',3)+3\nsrc='''\"\"\"Held-lead duration on a running heads-minus-tails tally.\n\nPeople expect a random coin's lead to keep changing hands: the running tally\nshould leave even and come back, again and again. A sequence in which one face\nstays ahead for a long unbroken stretch (the tally not returning to even for\nmany flips, however small the lead) looks stuck and less random, by a shared\npenalty on the longest stretch the lead is held, as a share of the length. The\nrest of the impression is the current best model's (tally span against a\npersonal expected span, switching against a personal ideal rate, chunk variety\nand a rule-built penalty scaled by a personal pattern sensitivity, the\nfinal-streak penalty, a personal left/right lean).\n\"\"\"'''+src[doc_end:]\nsrc=src.replace('''    a = sequence_a.strip().upper()''','''    def held_lead(seq):\n        # Longest stretch of flips with the tally away from even, / length.\n        tally, cur, best = 0, 0, 0\n        for c in seq:\n            tally += 1 if c == \"H\" else -1\n            cur = cur + 1 if tally != 0 else 0\n            best = max(best, cur)\n        return best / len(seq)\n\n    a = sequence_a.strip().upper()''')\nsrc=src.replace('''        \"log_len\": float''','''        \"lead_diff\": held_lead(a) - held_lead(b),\n        \"log_len\": float''')\nsrc=src.replace('''    log_len = pm.Data(\"log_len\"''','''    lead_diff = pm.Data(\"lead_diff\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\"))\n    log_len = pm.Data(\"log_len\"''')\nsrc=src.replace('''    # Person-specific left/right''','''    # The claim: shared penalty on the longest stretch a lead is held.\n    omega = pm.Normal(\"omega\", mu=0.0, sigma=2.0)\n\n    # Person-specific left/right''')\nsrc=src.replace('''        - tau * term_diff\n''','''        - tau * term_diff\n        - omega * lead_diff\n''')\nopen(\"iter_4/candidate_0/candidate.py\",\"w\").write(src)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"lead\\|omega\" iter_4/candidate_0/candidate.py | head -20\npython3 -c \"\nimport sys; sys.path.insert(0,'iter_4/candidate_0')\n\" ; cd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run2/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir $D --responses /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5\" completed (exit code 0)","uuid":"47170648-c59a-4137-ab8d-fff4681dfb8c","session_id":"3dce34f6-6e85-412b-9be4-6e3bf4af1a3e"}
