{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfh18PN8G2R1exN3hsDbz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written the candidate as **`held_lead_duration_tally`**, and the self-check printed `OK`. In its short smoke fit (one chain, 100 draws) the ELPD-LOO was −3259.6, against −3262.5 for the current best model's full fit. That comparison is only a hint, since the fits aren't comparable. The check doesn't test novelty, convergence or the 30-minute fit limit, so those are still open until admission.\n\n**Hypothesis.** People keep a running count of how far heads lead tails and expect a random coin's lead to keep changing hands. If one face stays ahead for a long unbroken stretch, the sequence looks stuck and less random, even when the lead never gets large. HHTHTHTH is an example: heads stay one or two ahead the whole way. This adds a shared penalty on the longest stretch the lead is held without the count getting back to even, as a share of the sequence length. It's different from the existing tally-span models, which only look at how far the count swings. This is the path-of-the-tally idea the brief asked for.\n\n**Model.** I copied the current best model, `terminal_streak_recency_pattern_rule`, and added one feature and one prior (`omega ~ Normal(0, 2)`). I checked the feature by hand: HHTHTHTH and HTHTTHTH have the same span and the same switch rate but differ by 0.875 on the new feature.\n\n**Risk.** This is an exploratory slot, which is meant to propose a new mechanism rather than build on an existing model. I kept the best model's other parts unchanged, following the pattern of other admitted exploratory models (`memory_span_limited_comparison`, `first_read_anchored_departure`). The new idea is only the held-lead penalty, but the model could still be read as an add-on to the incumbent. If the fit drives `omega` near zero, it will also fail the novelty check as a near-duplicate of the incumbent.\n\nFiles are in `/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_4/candidate_0`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2289,"cache_read_input_tokens":89393,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2289,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":713,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3dce34f6-6e85-412b-9be4-6e3bf4af1a3e","uuid":"d5811ef3-a7c6-4575-906b-66f2cdb798e7","timestamp":"2026-10-04T10:01:01.093Z","request_id":"req_011Cfh18NZ1JX9hgV5XyTtAn"}
